{{/*
HTML viewer for the JSON Schema of crdkit.schema.jsonSchema.

The viewer is a fixed shell (CSS + JS) that reads the schema embedded in
the page, so a schema or example change changes only the embedded JSON.
One file, system fonts, no external request; light and dark follow
prefers-color-scheme.
*/}}

{{/*
crdkit.schema.html (public)

Renders a JSON Schema generated by crdkit.schema.jsonSchema as a
self-contained, interactive HTML values reference.

Interface:
- Params (dict): { "schema": <JSON Schema text>, "title": <page title,
  optional — default the schema's title, else "Values"> }
- Returns: the HTML document as plain text.

Implementation notes:
- The schema is embedded compact (re-encoded with toJson) as `<script
  type="application/json" id="crdkit-schema">`, every `</` written as
  `<\/`.
- The viewer follows the same generated-example rules as
  crdkit.schema.generatedExample.internal, so the HTML and the Markdown
  agree.
*/}}
{{- define "crdkit.schema.html" -}}
{{- $schema := .schema | default "{}" -}}
{{- $js := $schema | fromJson -}}
{{- $title := .title | default $js.title | default "Values" -}}
{{- include "crdkit.schema.viewer.internal" (dict "title" $title "json" ($js | toJson)) -}}
{{- end -}}
